  "findings": "Inspected the low arching stand and twice-divided frond photographs, then all three current pilots and 36 variants. Curved rachises carry aligned pinnae and pinnules; the species has a more open arching frond range than the male fern source. Current heights span 0.28-0.70 m. The small end merges fine pinnules into stepped blades at 25 mm, while larger variants show separated divisions; microscopic sori and margin teeth are omitted. Accepted as stylized spring lady fern, pending user endorsement.",
